# Build context sent to Cloud Build / the Docker daemon.
#
# This file is a security boundary, not an optimisation. Without it,
# `gcloud builds submit` from this directory uploads `.env` and
# `secrets/firebase-admin.json` — a live Firebase Admin private key that can mint
# credentials for any user in the project — to Cloud Build. The Dockerfile never
# COPYs them, so the image stays clean either way; the point is that they must not
# leave the machine in the first place.

# Credentials and configuration
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Python build artefacts and local virtualenv
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Tool caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Not needed at runtime. The Dockerfile copies only app/, alembic/, alembic.ini,
# pyproject.toml and uv.lock; everything else here is context weight.
# The Dockerfile itself is deliberately NOT ignored: `gcloud builds submit` uploads
# this context as a tarball and Cloud Build then looks for the Dockerfile inside it.
tests/
docs/
*.md
docker-compose.yml
Makefile

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
